<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gangadhar Rao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1853</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gangadhar Rao was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> Raja of Jhansi of the Newalkar family, who ruled until his death in 1853. He married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lakshmibai">Manikarnika</a>, later famous as Rani Lakshmibai. Shortly before his death he adopted a son, Damodar Rao, but the governor-general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lord-dalhousie">Lord Dalhousie</a> refused to recognise the adoption and annexed Jhansi under the doctrine of lapse in 1854.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gangadhar-rao.jpg" alt="Gangadhar Rao" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gangadhar_Rao_alias_Babasaheb_Newalkar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
